    <briefdescription>
<para>Computes a weight and dates/indices for linearly interpolating between two dates. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Bruce Wyman</para></simplesect>
A time type is converted into two consecutive dates plus a fraction representing the distance between the dates. This information can be used to interpolate between the dates. The dates may be expressed as years, months, or days or as indices in an array. </para>    </detaileddescription>
